vcl: a font answers to its family name in every language

A font names its family in several languages: Source Han Serif SC is
also "思源宋体". Each platform keeps one of the names: Windows the
one for the system locale, macOS the one for the UI language,
fontconfig the one for the kernel's UI language. A document from WPS
asks for "思源宋体". On Windows and macOS the lookup missed whenever
the kept name was the other one, and the text fell back to another
font. On Linux fontconfig found the font, but the fonts-missing
check compared "思源宋体" with "Source Han Serif SC" and reported it
missing (Ely #82).

The lookup now tries the family names (name IDs 1 and 16, every
language) read from the fonts' name tables, once, on the first
document font name it misses; the time it took goes to the log. The
check names a used face by the document's name when the face carries
that name.
